# env
#
# .env.local was previously COMMITTED, pointing NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL at
# http://localhost:4000/api. Vercel's own variables do win over it — Next.js
# does not overwrite an entry already in process.env — but committing it made a
# missing Vercel variable fail SILENTLY, falling back to localhost instead of
# failing the build. Untracked, a forgotten variable is loud.
#
# See .env.production.example for the values a deployment needs.
.env.local
.env*.local.bak
